  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\nIssued at 1233 PM CDT MON AUG 24 2026\n\nIsolated showers and thunderstorms have been developing late this\nmorning to the south of a stalled boundary across our far\nsouthern CWA. Similar to the last few days, an upper level\nshortwave will rotate through the region between a trough to our\nnortheast and a ridge out to our west. This will help trigger\nadditional convection across our southern areas through the\nafternoon and evening hours. As we warm up through the day,\nconditions will become favorable for damaging wind gusts. There\nis low risk for more organized convection across our southwestern\ncounties as storms move south across Mississippi through the day.\nActivity will become more isolated across our southeastern areas.\nTherefore, SPC maintains a Marginal Risk (Level 1 out of 5) for \nsevere storms across the southern half of the state through late \nthis evening. The lingering boundary will begin to lift north late\nin the day Tuesday, spreading deeper moisture back north across \nthe state. Before it begins its journey, another round of isolated\nconvection is likely across the southern part of Alabama. \nDamaging wind gusts will be the primary concern with this \nactivity. In addition to the severe threat, high PWATs (around 2\")\nwill support heavy rainfall with any storm, leading to isolated \ninstances of flash flooding. \n\nBy mid week, another upper trough deepens across the Great Lakes \nregion while sending a cold front into Central Alabama sometime \nThursday into Friday. As a result, we will see low to moderate \n(30-70%) chances for showers and storms late this work week and \ninto the weekend. \n\nHigh temperatures this weekend will settle into the low to mid \n90s for most. Drier air will help keep heat indices in check, \ngenerally 95-102 degrees. Continued humid conditions will warrant \na low to moderate heat risk for most through the next week.\n\n95/Castillo",
